# .dockerignore — shrink the Docker/Podman build context for the service images.
#
# The service Dockerfiles (infra/docker/{ac,gc,mc,mh}-service/Dockerfile) are cargo-chef
# multi-stage builds that `COPY . .` from this repo root (the build CONTEXT is
# ${PROJECT_ROOT}; see infra/kind/scripts/setup.sh:build_image and the host-side helper's
# cmd_rebuild in crates/devloop-helper/src/commands.rs). Without this file the context
# includes the ~27 GB host `target/`, which (×4 services, no GC) exhausts the host
# container-storage filesystem mid-COPY ("no space left on device"). cargo-chef compiles
# fresh in the container's own /build/target, so the host build artifacts are NEVER read —
# excluding them is provably safe and only shrinks the context.
#
# Honored by BOTH engines: docker reads `.dockerignore`; podman/buildah read
# `.containerignore` first, then fall back to `.dockerignore` — so this single file covers
# both (the runtime is podman-or-docker per the detected KIND_EXPERIMENTAL_PROVIDER). The
# ignore file is read from the CONTEXT ROOT (= repo root here), not next to the -f Dockerfile.
#
# RULE: exclude build-irrelevant trees ONLY. Everything the cargo-chef build reads MUST
# stay: Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/** (sources + build.rs), proto/** (proto-gen/build.rs
# compiles ../../proto/), migrations/** (the runtime stage COPYs /build/migrations), .cargo/,
# .sqlx/. Patterns below are disjoint from those, so no negation (!) rules are needed.

# --- Rust build artifacts (the 27 GB keystone) ---
target/
**/target/

# --- VCS history (never a build input) ---
.git/

# --- JS/TS toolchain (the Rust services never read these) ---
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
**/.pnpm-store/
.nx/
packages/
dist/
build/
out/

# --- Coverage / profiling outputs ---
coverage/
.nyc_output/
lcov.info
*.profraw
*.profdata

# --- Docs, IaC state, editor/OS cruft (not build inputs) ---
docs/
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs ---
*.log
logs/

# --- Local env / secrets (never ship into the build context) ---
.env
.env.*

# --- Sibling worktrees (live outside this context; listed defensively) ---
worktrees/
